  "text": "Cathaír Mór, also spelled Cathaoir Mór, is an Irish hero. He ruled the land before Conn of the Hundred Battles. Conn came to the kingship of Tara. The name Cathaír means great battle-lord. Writers recorded little about this king. Conn pushed him from power and killed him. Cathaír was father of several noted women.",
